What would you do if the source schema suddenly changes?

Compare the incoming schema with the expected schema. 
Identify whether a column was added, removed, renamed, or had its data type changed.

Check whether the change is backward-compatible. Adding an optional column is generally easier to handle 
than changing customer_id from an integer to a string.

Step 3: Apply schema evolution if approved
If the new column is expected and approved, update the transformation logic and target schema.
In Databricks, Delta Lake supports schema evolution for compatible changes.

